   Carved from the tokens.css cascade root; @import-ed by tokens.css in
   cascade order. Same :root cascade context as its siblings. */
:root {
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       §-1  COLOR-SCHEME (AQ.W2 §1)

       Lets native UI (scrollbars, spinbuttons, form-control chrome, the
       default focus ring) honor the OS preference when the consumer has
       NOT pinned a `.dark` class. glass-ui's dark mode is class-driven
       (`.dark`, theme.css `@variant dark`), so `.dark` overrides to a hard
       `dark` regardless of OS — but absent the class, native chrome should
       still track `prefers-color-scheme`. `light dark` (not `only light`)
       on `:root` delivers that; `.dark` hard-pins `dark`.

       Baseline Widely Available → adopt natively, no `@supports` guard
       (older engines ignore the property and keep default-light chrome).
       `accent-color` (AQ.W2 §4) is the companion native-control brand;
       both are inherited built-in <color>/keyword properties re-specified
       inside `.dark`. The `--accent-color` token is defined in the §5
       color block below (custom properties resolve order-independently).
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ */
    color-scheme: light dark;
    accent-color: var(--accent-color);

    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       §0  FONT TOKEN SOURCE-OF-TRUTH

       The single authoritative declaration of the library's font register.
       theme.css bridges each --font-stack-* to its Tailwind --font-* namespace
       var; typography.css consumes the bridged --font-* names. The public
       runtime knobs remain --font-*, --leading-*, --tracking-*.

       ONE brand register: Plus Jakarta Sans (text + display) + Fira Code (mono).
       --font-stack-text drives the body/heading/prose/display register — the
       library DEFAULT is the register every live surface paints (the demo +
       speedtest render Plus Jakarta everywhere). The calibrated \"Plus Jakarta
       Sans Fallback\" / \"Fira Code Fallback\" faces (declared in typography.css)
       wrap the system stacks with Capsize metric overrides so the swap window
       is geometry-neutral (zero CLS). --font-stack-display aliases the text
       register: there is no separate display-serif voice. */
    --font-stack-text: \"Plus Jakarta Sans\", \"Plus Jakarta Sans Fallback\", system-ui, sans-serif;
    --font-stack-display: var(--font-stack-text);
    --font-stack-sans: var(--font-stack-text);
    --font-stack-mono: \"Fira Code\", \"Fira Code Fallback\", \"Fira Mono\", monospace;

    --type-leading-micro: 1.2;
    --type-leading-caption: 1.3;
    --type-leading-small: 1.4;
    --type-leading-body: 1.5;
    --type-leading-prose: 1.618;
    --type-leading-heading: 1.2;
